This slide is about Generative Adversarial Networks (GANs), a popular Deep Learning model used to create new images, videos, faces, artwork, and more.

What is GAN?

GAN consists of two neural networks:

Generator
Creates fake images.
Tries to make them look real.
Discriminator
Checks whether an image is real or fake.
Acts like a judge.

Both networks compete with each other, and over time the Generator becomes very good at creating realistic images.

Simple Example

Imagine:

A student drawing fake currency notes (Generator).
A teacher checking if the notes are real or fake (Discriminator).

The student improves after every mistake until the fake note looks almost real.

